  "caveats": [
    "The dominant error term is SHAPE, not offset: mean offset share is 0.05-0.10, scale 0.20-0.27, shape 0.65-0.76. The EXT-1 plan text assumed offset would dominate; that assumption is falsified by this artifact.",
    "Pooled Spearman is positive in all four endpoint x split cells (0.06-0.30), so rank transfer is not zero -- it is weak.",
    "Predictions are compressed: predicted sd is 0.31-0.54 against observed 0.64-0.96, slope 0.24-1.16 (four of five metals below 0.7). Part of the negative R2 is compression, which calibration can repair; the rest is ranking.",
    "calibration_ceiling_r2 = rho^2 is the R2 an infinite-sample linear recalibration would reach. It bounds every k-shot result in EXT-3.",
    "The centred arm centres the held-out metal's targets by that metal's own mean. This is an oracle operation that defines the shape estimand; it is not deployable. Deploying it requires estimating the mean from k measurements (EXT-3).",
    "The within-metal ceiling uses the same descriptors-only representation for comparability; a one-hot metal block would score slightly higher within metal.",
    "Censored rows are dropped (potency 18.4%), so every fit is on the potent side of each cohort.",
    "Five test cohorts differ in size and ligand chemistry; the per-metal numbers are not exchangeable."
  ]
}
